sers/JaredGivens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JaredGivens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-04T09:44:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-04T10:05:19Z","body":"Thanks for taking the time to make a test project that was super helpful!\r\n\r\nYou’re right that GPUParticles3D isn’t affected at all, and that’s expected: GPUParticles3D does not use MultiMesh internally. Particle trails do use MultiMesh though, so I just tweaked your test project to use a trail instead and attached the updated version now the effect is visible.\r\n\r\nThe PR also stopped multiplying the instance transform by the mvp transform. That was something I needed in my game, but it’s out of scope for this PR. But a change to add an explicit way to stop instance matrix multiplication could be a nice follow-up feature.\r\n\r\n[test_instance_matrix.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23928258/test_instance_matrix.zip)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3611142765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3693928475","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110909#issuecomment-3693928475","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110909","id":3693928475,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cLOAb","user":{"login":"rschyboll","id":73661977,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNjYxOTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73661977?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll","html_url":"https://github.com/rschyboll","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rschyboll/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-27T11:51:49Z","updated_at":"2025-12-27T11:51:49Z","body":"Is adding MULTIMESH_TRANSFORM_SKIP from the original PR still planned? Adding INSTANCE_MATRIX allows for more flexibility, but by itself it doesn’t seem to reduce the allocated memory per MultiMesh instance. Or did I not understand what exactly this PR does?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3693928475/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]